{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggyTWfSXHdaAuisgHzpm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The harness drives copies with random arrow/WASD keys and needs a same-origin server to check server-hosted and host-leave rounds. I'm looking up the engine API names the plan relies on next.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4979,"cache_read_input_tokens":153784,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4979},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01565e32-5dd5-4107-91e6-1b53667edea6","uuid":"bf50a2e8-4fdd-49d2-83cf-4cdef4db7533","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:54:14.582Z","request_id":"req_011CggyTWR4EHSvV7uvL2aF9","narration_block_indexes":[0],"thinking_duration_ms":1,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggyTWfSXHdaAuisgHzpm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XmH1cmpbJwBthkyC8RJwUn","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/.cache/gauntlet-plan-research-x8cc180/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff && grep -n -i \"slider\\|glyph\\|symbols\\|padAim\\|lastDevice\\|touchEnabled\\|allowJoin\\|addPlayer\\|removePlayer\\|autoPause\\|pausable\\|cam.frame\\|frame(\" API-INDEX.md | head -60","description":"Search API index for input, players, pause names"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4979,"cache_read_input_tokens":153784,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4979},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01565e32-5dd5-4107-91e6-1b53667edea6","uuid":"290625b7-3786-4841-84c5-690fd8a412ab","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:54:15.223Z","request_id":"req_011CggyTWR4EHSvV7uvL2aF9","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01XmH1cmpbJwBthkyC8RJwUn":{"command":"cd /home/micha/.cache/gauntlet-plan-research-x8cc180/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff && grep -n -i \"slider\\|glyph\\|symbols\\|padAim\\|lastDevice\\|touchEnabled\\|allowJoin\\|addPlayer\\|removePlayer\\|autoPause\\|pausable\\|cam.frame\\|frame(\" API-INDEX.md | head -60","description":"Search API index for input, players, pause names"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XmH1cmpbJwBthkyC8RJwUn","type":"tool_result","content":"215:- `E.anim(frames, fps = 8, o = {})` †: frames to play: anim([spr1, spr2, spr3], fps = 8, { loop: true, pingpong: false }), or anim(sheet, 8, { frames: 4 }) for several frames side by side in one sprite's rows. Draw it with r.sprite(x, y, z, a, { t }) (t: its clock, seconds; the game's time by default); a.frame(t) is the sprite at time t, a.index(t) its number, a.duration one play (seconds)\n283:- `input.codeLabel(code)`: a code as a person reads it: 'W' (or the keyboard's own letter there), 'Space', '↑', 'Left click', and a gamepad button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks the family)\n292:- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), with their bindings: input.label('jump') -> 'Space', 'A' or '✕'\n297:- `input.padStyle()`: the controller family whose symbols label() shows: glyphs, or with glyphs 'auto' the one its name says\n317:- `input.touchButtons(actions, o = {})` †: On-screen buttons for phones and tablets (shown on touch screens; the player's settings can show them always or hide them, put them on the left, and size them): input.touchButtons(['jump', 'attack'], { labels: { jump: 'A', attack: 'B' }, force }). The other half of the screen is a move stick (past halfway it presses up, down, left and right too, as a d-pad does: menus and ladders). START is the corner's menu button, top right: it opens the menu, or pauses a pausable scene into it (without the corner a START button there starts a title and pauses, as a gamepad's Start)\n326:- `input.glyphs = 'auto'`: the gamepad's button symbols for label(): 'auto' (from the controller's name) | 'xbox' | 'playstation' | 'nintendo' | 'generic' (positions)\n329:- `input.lastDevice = 'keyboard'`: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch', the last one used (show the right button prompts)\n334:- `input.padAim = null` †: its right stick, or null when centered\n337:- `input.padLost = false`: true for the step after the gamepad in use was unplugged (a pausable scene pauses)\n350:- `input.touchEnabled = true` †: false turns the touch stick off\n360:- `E.font.title(g, s, x, y, o = {})`: Big logo text for title screens: scaled glyphs with a vertical color gradient, an outline and an extruded 3D edge. title(g, 'CASTLE OF NIGHT', x, y, { scale: 3, colors: ['#fff6c8', '#ffd36a', '#e07a2a'], outline: '#1a0c10', depth: 3, depthColor: '#6a2a1a', align: 'center' })\n453:- `new E.Game(o = {}) → game`: new E.Game({ canvas, view, views, res, expand, input, bg, step: 1 / 120, loop: true, headless: false, menu, fullscreen: 'tap', corner: true, backGesture: true, autoPause: true, id, pace, camera }). The standard features (section 10b) every game gets: menu, fullscreen, corner, backGesture, autoPause.\n462:- `new E.Game({ autoPause })`: a pausable scene pauses when the page is hidden or loses focus\n468:- `game.addPlayer(o = {})` †: a player in now: { pad: index } (a gamepad) or { keys: 'right' } (the keyboard's right half; player 1 takes the left). Returns its input (null when four play already)\n471:- `game.allowJoin(o = {})` †: let players join, up to max (2..4): Start on a gamepad no one holds, or 2 on the keyboard (o.keys: false not); onJoin (input, number) as each does. allowJoin(false) closes it (the names split and join are String's and Array's)\n484:- `game.menu(name)`: open the menu (the corner's menu button and the touch START do it): a pausable scene (or a game started without scenes) pauses on its pause screen; any other scene, a title, waits under the settings. menu('settings') or menu('controls') opens that screen. Without a menu (menu: false, or the agent edition) it pauses a scene in play. Returns true when a menu opened\n490:- `game.players` †: the players: [game.input (player 1), ...the ones who joined (game.allowJoin, game.addPlayer: section 10j)]; each an input with player (1..4), name ('P1'), color (E.PLAYER_COLORS) and device. A game of one: [game.input]\n491:- `game.removePlayer(p)` †: a player leaves (its input, or its number, 2 to 4); player 1 has the whole keyboard back when no one shares it\n502:- `game.start(hooks)`: Start the loop. Either one scene: game.start({ update(dt), draw(r) }) or several: game.start({ scenes: { title: {...}, play: {...} }, scene: 'title' }) A scene is { enter(data), exit(), update(dt), draw(r), back(), pausable, view, views, input, res, expand, touch, camera } (all optional). start() with nothing resumes a stopped loop. A headless game, or one made with loop: false, runs only by advance().\n518:- `game.cam`: camera. smooth = seconds of lag; bounds(view) = clamp rect; room = [w, h] world units for screen-by-screen rooms; moving = sliding between rooms; offset = [dx, dy] screen pixels from the screen's centre to where the focus sits (above a phone's touch buttons: [0, -40]); x, y: the camera's position in projected pixels (its top-left corner); vx, vy: how fast it is moving there; tx, ty, tz: the world point it is following (focus sets it); snap: true makes it jump there at the next step instead of gliding (a new level, a teleport); window: [w, h] screen pixels, a dead zone round the focus it moves in before the camera follows (Super Mario World's; [48, 0] for sideways only); snapY: true follows a followed body's height only when it lands (onGround) or nears the screen's edge (side-scrollers); frame(targets, { margin: 24, zoom: [min, max] or false }) keeps every one of them (anything with x, y, z) in view, centered between them and zoomed out (no further than min) when they spread apart, until frame(null); free: a free camera (strategy, sims, board games): true or { keys: true, edge: 10, drag: true, speed: 300, bounds: [x0, y0, x1, y1] }: the keys or a pad's stick pan it (input.move(), speed screen pixels a second), the mouse at the screen's edge (within edge pixels), a drag (input.pan(): a finger on open ground, a mouse's middle or right button) one to one; a zoom (wheel, pinch) zooms toward the pointer or the pinch; its focus keeps to bounds (world x, y); focus() still moves it; in every view and turn; null (as it starts): off\n536:- `game.paused = false`: true while paused (a pausable scene toggles it on 'pause'; steps still run, scenes don't update)\n565:- `settings.define(sp)`: add a setting: { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', value, min, max, step, options: [[value, label]] or [value], help, group: 'Game', apply(game, value) }. Its saved value is loaded (when it is a valid one) and applied; it shows on the settings screen. Returns its value\n568:- `settings.set(key, v)`: change a setting: checked (a slider kept in range, a choice among its options), saved, applied, onChange told. Returns the value kept (the old one when v is not a valid value)\n1166:- `new E.Shell({ settings })`: settings.items: the game's own settings, { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', min, max, step, options, value } (kept in game.settings, beside the standard ones)\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174804__x8cc180/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01565e32-5dd5-4107-91e6-1b53667edea6","uuid":"2680400e-5b0c-4ec9-b123-35e8da2c15ee","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:54:15.249Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"215:- `E.anim(frames, fps = 8, o = {})` †: frames to play: anim([spr1, spr2, spr3], fps = 8, { loop: true, pingpong: false }), or anim(sheet, 8, { frames: 4 }) for several frames side by side in one sprite's rows. Draw it with r.sprite(x, y, z, a, { t }) (t: its clock, seconds; the game's time by default); a.frame(t) is the sprite at time t, a.index(t) its number, a.duration one play (seconds)\n283:- `input.codeLabel(code)`: a code as a person reads it: 'W' (or the keyboard's own letter there), 'Space', '↑', 'Left click', and a gamepad button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks the family)\n292:- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), with their bindings: input.label('jump') -> 'Space', 'A' or '✕'\n297:- `input.padStyle()`: the controller family whose symbols label() shows: glyphs, or with glyphs 'auto' the one its name says\n317:- `input.touchButtons(actions, o = {})` †: On-screen buttons for phones and tablets (shown on touch screens; the player's settings can show them always or hide them, put them on the left, and size them): input.touchButtons(['jump', 'attack'], { labels: { jump: 'A', attack: 'B' }, force }). The other half of the screen is a move stick (past halfway it presses up, down, left and right too, as a d-pad does: menus and ladders). START is the corner's menu button, top right: it opens the menu, or pauses a pausable scene into it (without the corner a START button there starts a title and pauses, as a gamepad's Start)\n326:- `input.glyphs = 'auto'`: the gamepad's button symbols for label(): 'auto' (from the controller's name) | 'xbox' | 'playstation' | 'nintendo' | 'generic' (positions)\n329:- `input.lastDevice = 'keyboard'`: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch', the last one used (show the right button prompts)\n334:- `input.padAim = null` †: its right stick, or null when centered\n337:- `input.padLost = false`: true for the step after the gamepad in use was unplugged (a pausable scene pauses)\n350:- `input.touchEnabled = true` †: false turns the touch stick off\n360:- `E.font.title(g, s, x, y, o = {})`: Big logo text for title screens: scaled glyphs with a vertical color gradient, an outline and an extruded 3D edge. title(g, 'CASTLE OF NIGHT', x, y, { scale: 3, colors: ['#fff6c8', '#ffd36a', '#e07a2a'], outline: '#1a0c10', depth: 3, depthColor: '#6a2a1a', align: 'center' })\n453:- `new E.Game(o = {}) → game`: new E.Game({ canvas, view, views, res, expand, input, bg, step: 1 / 120, loop: true, headless: false, menu, fullscreen: 'tap', corner: true, backGesture: true, autoPause: true, id, pace, camera }). The standard features (section 10b) every game gets: menu, fullscreen, corner, backGesture, autoPause.\n462:- `new E.Game({ autoPause })`: a pausable scene pauses when the page is hidden or loses focus\n468:- `game.addPlayer(o = {})` †: a player in now: { pad: index } (a gamepad) or { keys: 'right' } (the keyboard's right half; player 1 takes the left). Returns its input (null when four play already)\n471:- `game.allowJoin(o = {})` †: let players join, up to max (2..4): Start on a gamepad no one holds, or 2 on the keyboard (o.keys: false not); onJoin (input, number) as each does. allowJoin(false) closes it (the names split and join are String's and Array's)\n484:- `game.menu(name)`: open the menu (the corner's menu button and the touch START do it): a pausable scene (or a game started without scenes) pauses on its pause screen; any other scene, a title, waits under the settings. menu('settings') or menu('controls') opens that screen. Without a menu (menu: false, or the agent edition) it pauses a scene in play. Returns true when a menu opened\n490:- `game.players` †: the players: [game.input (player 1), ...the ones who joined (game.allowJoin, game.addPlayer: section 10j)]; each an input with player (1..4), name ('P1'), color (E.PLAYER_COLORS) and device. A game of one: [game.input]\n491:- `game.removePlayer(p)` †: a player leaves (its input, or its number, 2 to 4); player 1 has the whole keyboard back when no one shares it\n502:- `game.start(hooks)`: Start the loop. Either one scene: game.start({ update(dt), draw(r) }) or several: game.start({ scenes: { title: {...}, play: {...} }, scene: 'title' }) A scene is { enter(data), exit(), update(dt), draw(r), back(), pausable, view, views, input, res, expand, touch, camera } (all optional). start() with nothing resumes a stopped loop. A headless game, or one made with loop: false, runs only by advance().\n518:- `game.cam`: camera. smooth = seconds of lag; bounds(view) = clamp rect; room = [w, h] world units for screen-by-screen rooms; moving = sliding between rooms; offset = [dx, dy] screen pixels from the screen's centre to where the focus sits (above a phone's touch buttons: [0, -40]); x, y: the camera's position in projected pixels (its top-left corner); vx, vy: how fast it is moving there; tx, ty, tz: the world point it is following (focus sets it); snap: true makes it jump there at the next step instead of gliding (a new level, a teleport); window: [w, h] screen pixels, a dead zone round the focus it moves in before the camera follows (Super Mario World's; [48, 0] for sideways only); snapY: true follows a followed body's height only when it lands (onGround) or nears the screen's edge (side-scrollers); frame(targets, { margin: 24, zoom: [min, max] or false }) keeps every one of them (anything with x, y, z) in view, centered between them and zoomed out (no further than min) when they spread apart, until frame(null); free: a free camera (strategy, sims, board games): true or { keys: true, edge: 10, drag: true, speed: 300, bounds: [x0, y0, x1, y1] }: the keys or a pad's stick pan it (input.move(), speed screen pixels a second), the mouse at the screen's edge (within edge pixels), a drag (input.pan(): a finger on open ground, a mouse's middle or right button) one to one; a zoom (wheel, pinch) zooms toward the pointer or the pinch; its focus keeps to bounds (world x, y); focus() still moves it; in every view and turn; null (as it starts): off\n536:- `game.paused = false`: true while paused (a pausable scene toggles it on 'pause'; steps still run, scenes don't update)\n565:- `settings.define(sp)`: add a setting: { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', value, min, max, step, options: [[value, label]] or [value], help, group: 'Game', apply(game, value) }. Its saved value is loaded (when it is a valid one) and applied; it shows on the settings screen. Returns its value\n568:- `settings.set(key, v)`: change a setting: checked (a slider kept in range, a choice among its options), saved, applied, onChange told. Returns the value kept (the old one when v is not a valid value)\n1166:- `new E.Shell({ settings })`: settings.items: the game's own settings, { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', min, max, step, options, value } (kept in game.settings, beside the standard ones)","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174804__x8cc180/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01XmH1cmpbJwBthkyC8RJwUn","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
