{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0117uTDKPG3KofSayHbjDMj7","type":"tool_result","content":"API-INDEX.md:323:- `input.aimSource = 'move'` †: what aims right now: 'move' | 'mouse' | 'pad'\nmy-3d2dge.js:762:     *  were down at the last step; aimSource: what aims right now: 'move' | 'mouse' | 'pad' */\nmy-3d2dge.js:763:    this.stick = [0, 0]; this.stickOn = false; this.padMove = [0, 0]; this.padAim = null; this.padPrev = []; this.aimSource = 'move';\nmy-3d2dge.js:825:    on(el, 'pointermove', e => { if (e.pointerType === 'mouse') { this.mouse.cx = e.clientX; this.mouse.cy = e.clientY; this.mouse.active = true; this.mouse.t = this.clock; this.aimSource = 'mouse'; this._fedAt = null; } else { this._pinchMove(e); this._stickMove(e); } if (this._g && this._g.id === e.pointerId) this._gesture('move', ...this.screenPoint(e.clientX, e.clientY)); });\nmy-3d2dge.js:829:      if (e.pointerType === 'mouse') { this.mouse.cx = e.clientX; this.mouse.cy = e.clientY; this.mouse.active = true; this.aimSource = 'mouse'; this.press('Mouse' + e.button); }\nmy-3d2dge.js:998:    if (code.startsWith('Pad')) { this.lastDevice = 'gamepad'; this.aimSource = 'pad'; }\nmy-3d2dge.js:1149:      if (this.aimSource === 'pad') this.aimSource = 'move';\nmy-3d2dge.js:1157:      if (this.padAim || Math.hypot(...this.padMove) > 0) { this.aimSource = 'pad'; this.lastDevice = 'gamepad'; }\nmy-3d2dge.js:1214:    this.screen.canvas.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId); this.aimSource = 'move'; this.lastDevice = 'touch';\nmy-3d2dge.js:3759:  const I = P[0], was = game._p1 || [I.lastDevice, I.padIndex, I.aimSource]; game._p1 = [I.lastDevice, I.padIndex, I.aimSource];\nmy-3d2dge.js:3768:    if (I.padIndex === p.index) { I.consumeAll(); [I.lastDevice, , I.aimSource] = was; game._p1 = was; }   // (that Start was the joiner's: player 1 neither pauses nor turns to the pad)\n20:- Collision, standing, sight (`map.sight`, `map.ray`), reach (`E.targets`, `E.inArc` with `dz`) and navigation (`E.FlowField`) all follow these rules. `E.dist` is 3D; `E.overlap` is flat.\n73:- 815 Flow field; E.FlowField: flow\n817:- `new E.FlowField(map, o = {}) → flow`: new E.FlowField(map, { step: 2, climb: 0, drop: 0, jump: 0 }): distances over the tops a body can stand on (E.HEIGHTS). With no options it covers the floor (and walls no higher than step, which bodies walk over); a target on a roof gets a field across the roofs it connects to\n818:- `new E.FlowField({ step, climb, drop })`: next-door cells connect when their tops differ by at most step, or going up by up to climb and down by up to drop (agents that climb walls or hop down)\n819:- `new E.FlowField({ jump })`: (world units) links tops across a gap that a jump clears, straight along a row or column, by map.landing's rules (up to jumpRise higher, 11, and jumpDrop lower, 18): an agent with E.Mover's leap chases across roofs. With jump, distances are travel: a jump of k cells costs k, and a climb 1 plus its rise in cells (climbing is slow), so a chase leaps a gap rather than drop into the street and climb back up\n820:- `flow.dir(x, y, fx, fy)`: normalized ground direction to walk from (x, y) toward the target (straight at it where the field doesn't reach)\n821:- `flow.next(x, y)` †: the next cell to head for from (x, y): { x, y, z (its center and top), kind: 'walk' | 'climb' | 'drop' | 'jump', edge (how far (x, y) is from the side of its cell it leaves by) }, or null where the field doesn't reach (or at the target). An AI standing on the ground presses jump for a 'climb' or a 'jump' once edge is under its radius plus a little (E.Mover climbs or leaps; a press in the air would be kept for the landing)\n822:- `flow.update(x, y)`: aim the field at a world point; it rebuilds only when the target's cell or the map (map.version) changes\n823:- `flow.climb`: how much higher a next-door top may be (an agent that climbs walls)\n824:- `flow.d`: each cell's distance in steps to the target cell (1e9 where it can't get