{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh21pfYCEMhzdj9ThSJH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NvNTsUdP6drTMF3ovd96Hx","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/.cache/gauntlet-plan-research-x8cc180/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff && grep -n \"toGround\\|unproject\\|screenToGround\\|groundAt(sx\\|screenToWorld\\|view.ground\" API-INDEX.md | head -10; sed -n 219,245p API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-260","description":"Find screen-to-ground conversion helpers in API"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1047,"cache_read_input_tokens":417018,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1047},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01565e32-5dd5-4107-91e6-1b53667edea6","uuid":"8ec7b283-d589-48e2-b534-bcb71c247a56","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:27:52.677Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh21pRQA6TzqMM5trk4R","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01NvNTsUdP6drTMF3ovd96Hx":{"command":"cd /home/micha/.cache/gauntlet-plan-research-x8cc180/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff && grep -n \"toGround\\|unproject\\|screenToGround\\|groundAt(sx\\|screenToWorld\\|view.ground\" API-INDEX.md | head -10; sed -n 219,245p API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-260","description":"Find screen-to-ground conversion helpers in API"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NvNTsUdP6drTMF3ovd96Hx","type":"tool_result","content":"229:- `view.toGround(sx, sy)`: projected screen point -> ground point (z = 0). null in side view\n## 3. Views (projections)\n\n- `E.VIEWS: iso, threequarter, topdown, brawler, side, overhead`: the ready-made views: iso (yaw 45, pitch 30), threequarter (pitch 55), topdown (80), brawler (25), side (0) and overhead (90, scale 1: world x/y = screen pixels); new E.Game({ view: 'iso' }) and\n- `E.VIEW_ORDER: iso, threequarter, topdown, brawler, side`: the order game.nextView() cycles through when a game doesn't set game.views ('overhead' is left out)\n- `new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale = 1, zBoost = 1) → view`: new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale, zBoost): an orthographic camera (degrees; scale = screen pixels per world unit; zBoost stretches heights)\n- `view.depth(x, y, z = 0)`: true camera depth: use it to sort parts inside one object\n- `view.order(x, y, z = 0)`: painter's order for whole objects standing on the ground\n- `view.p(x, y, z = 0)`: world -> projected screen pixels (not yet camera-relative)\n- `view.screenDirToGround(dx, dy)`: a direction the player pushed on screen (x right, y down) -> normalized ground direction\n- `view.set(yaw, pitch, scale = 1, zBoost = 1)`: change the angles and scale in place (game.setView and rotateView use their own copies); returns the view\n- `view.toGround(sx, sy)`: projected screen point -> ground point (z = 0). null in side view\n- `view.ax`, `view.ay`: screen x = ax * x + ay * y (the projection's first row)\n- `view.bx`, `view.by`, `view.bz`: screen y = bx * x + by * y + bz * z (the second row; bz < 0 lifts things up the screen)\n- `view.dx`, `view.dy`, `view.dz`: the direction toward the camera, for true depth (view.depth)\n- `view.fx`, `view.fy`: the ground direction that points at the camera (the front of a wall faces it)\n- `view.id`: its name ('iso', or yours)\n- `view.inv`: the inverse of the ground projection (screen -> ground at z 0), null in side views\n- `view.isSide`: a side view (pitch 1 or less: x right, z up, y is depth)\n- `view.isTop`: looking straight down (pitch 89 or more)\n- `view.label`: its name for people ('Isometric')\n- `view.pitch`, `view.yaw`: the same angles in radians\n- `view.pitchDeg`: the tilt, 0 side view to 90 straight down\n- `view.scale`: screen pixels per world unit\n- `view.yawDeg`: the turn about the up axis, degrees (0: north is up the screen; iso is 45)\n- `view.zBoost`: how much heights are stretched on screen (1 = true)\n- `E.charView(view)`: the view a rig in `view` is drawn from (the sprite-like angle above; the view itself outside pitch 40-89)\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174804__x8cc180/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01565e32-5dd5-4107-91e6-1b53667edea6","uuid":"3bdd2b8e-c9f7-4e81-b88f-c6a17e08951b","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:27:52.694Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"229:- `view.toGround(sx, sy)`: projected screen point -> ground point (z = 0). null in side view\n## 3. Views (projections)\n\n- `E.VIEWS: iso, threequarter, topdown, brawler, side, overhead`: the ready-made views: iso (yaw 45, pitch 30), threequarter (pitch 55), topdown (80), brawler (25), side (0) and overhead (90, scale 1: world x/y = screen pixels); new E.Game({ view: 'iso' }) and\n- `E.VIEW_ORDER: iso, threequarter, topdown, brawler, side`: the order game.nextView() cycles through when a game doesn't set game.views ('overhead' is left out)\n- `new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale = 1, zBoost = 1) → view`: new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale, zBoost): an orthographic camera (degrees; scale = screen pixels per world unit; zBoost stretches heights)\n- `view.depth(x, y, z = 0)`: true camera depth: use it to sort parts inside one object\n- `view.order(x, y, z = 0)`: painter's order for whole objects standing on the ground\n- `view.p(x, y, z = 0)`: world -> projected screen pixels (not yet camera-relative)\n- `view.screenDirToGround(dx, dy)`: a direction the player pushed on screen (x right, y down) -> normalized ground direction\n- `view.set(yaw, pitch, scale = 1, zBoost = 1)`: change the angles and scale in place (game.setView and rotateView use their own copies); returns the view\n- `view.toGround(sx, sy)`: projected screen point -> ground point (z = 0). null in side view\n- `view.ax`, `view.ay`: screen x = ax * x + ay * y (the projection's first row)\n- `view.bx`, `view.by`, `view.bz`: screen y = bx * x + by * y + bz * z (the second row; bz < 0 lifts things up the screen)\n- `view.dx`, `view.dy`, `view.dz`: the direction toward the camera, for true depth (view.depth)\n- `view.fx`, `view.fy`: the ground direction that points at the camera (the front of a wall faces it)\n- `view.id`: its name ('iso', or yours)\n- `view.inv`: the inverse of the ground projection (screen -> ground at z 0), null in side views\n- `view.isSide`: a side view (pitch 1 or less: x right, z up, y is depth)\n- `view.isTop`: looking straight down (pitch 89 or more)\n- `view.label`: its name for people ('Isometric')\n- `view.pitch`, `view.yaw`: the same angles in radians\n- `view.pitchDeg`: the tilt, 0 side view to 90 straight down\n- `view.scale`: screen pixels per world unit\n- `view.yawDeg`: the turn about the up axis, degrees (0: north is up the screen; iso is 45)\n- `view.zBoost`: how much heights are stretched on screen (1 = true)\n- `E.charView(view)`: the view a rig in `view` is drawn from (the sprite-like angle above; the view itself outside pitch 40-89)","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174804__x8cc180/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NvNTsUdP6drTMF3ovd96Hx","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
