{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xj2gfTNX5RWYpwmkWWKRxg","type":"tool_result","content":"140\t| `05-text.js` | All player-facing text: narrator lines (5.6), story (5.1), floor intros, How to Play cards, class quips, About/Credits pages (Source Information and feedback filled in at the end) |\n141\t| `10-heroes.js` | `def('heroes', ...)` ×4: stats, rig factory, shot, melee moves, magic power, voice |\n142\t| `11-monsters.js` | `def('monsters', ...)` ×7 and `def('boss', 'famish', ...)`: stats per rank, AI kind, rig factory, generator kind, score |\n143\t| `12-items.js` | `def('items', ...)` for every pickup, 7 special potions, 5 amulets: art, effect, shootable or not, points |\n144\t| `13-art.js` | New art: string sprites, `E.SHAPES` entries (generators with damage states, doors, stairs, plates, pads, runes, pylons, bell, jug, platter, tureen), the `Shade` ghost rig class, realm palettes and materials |\n145\t| `15..18-floors-*.js` | `def('floors', ...)`: rows and meta for each floor (5.5), one file per realm plus the banquet |\n146\t| `20-level.js` | Floor parser (legend → TileMap, entity lists, door groups, trap groups, transporter pairs, exits, beams); automatic decoration (torches, props) from a hash; lights list; **`validateFloor()`**, shared with the tests |\n147\t| `21-sim.js` | The world (`W`): state, step order, damage pipeline, scoring, kill and pickup events |\n148\t| `22-sim-heroes.js` | Hero controller: intent → movement, aim, fire, smart melee, plant, magic; drain; pickups; doors; stairs; death and rising; amulets and specials |\n149\t| `23-sim-monsters.js` | Monster AI kinds, flow fields (multi-source and single-source), separation, ranks |\n150\t| `24-sim-generators.js` | Spawning, ranks, damage states, caps |\n151\t| `25-sim-features.js` | Traps, transporters, stun runes, force fields, spikes, cracked and fake walls, impatience, treasure-room clock |\n152\t| `26-sim-boss.js` | King Famish's fight as an `E.Script` (phases, attacks, waves, feast) |\n153\t| `30-intents.js` | Intents from a local player's input (keyboard, mouse, gamepad), from the network, from the bot |\n154\t| `31-bot.js` | The autopilot (attract mode, playthrough tests, Dev \"bot plays P1\") |\n155\t| `40-net.js` | Net roles: local, host, client, server; snapshot and event encoding; client puppets and interpolation; rate limiting; area of interest |\n156\t| `41-session.js` | The AI Hub flow: connect, own card, ready, start countdown, time-up, finish, end, leave |\n157\t| `50-view.js` | Drawing: floor and walls, decoration, lights, entities (from the sim or from puppets), projectiles, reticle, x-ray, debug overlays |\n158\t| `51-hud.js` | Player panels, captions, floor and realm cards, timers, edge arrows, prompts |\n159\t| `52-narrator.js` | The callout queue: priority, cooldowns, captions, voice |\n160\t| `53-audio.js` | Songs, sound-effect definitions, the **Babble** voice synth, dynamic music layers |\n161\t| `60-scenes-front.js` | Title, main menu, class select, How to Play, High Scores, About/Credits, the touch-only notice |\n162\t| `61-scenes-play.js` | Play (solo and local co-op), floor cards, treasure rooms, game over, continue, initials, ending, credits, Descent II |\n163\t| `62-scenes-session.js` | Session scenes: card, countdown, play, round over, server |\n164\t| `63-attract.js` | The attract-mode director |\n165\t| `70-dev.js` | Dev Tools: cheats, warp, give and spawn, tuning sliders, overlays |\n166\t| `80-debug.js` | `game.debug` (snapshot, teleport, warp, give, spawn, setTune, bot, netStats) and `game.stateHash` |\n167\t| `99-start.js` | `game.start({ scenes, scene, boot })` |\n168\t\n169\tContent never edits the core: floors, monsters, items and lines are registry entries (the Emberdeep lesson), so the rest of the game can be built later by adding data in a text editor (`docs/DESIGNER.md` explains how).\n170\t\n171\t### 3.3 Runtime model: simulation, intents, view, network\n172\t\n173\t```\n174\t           +---------------- intents ----------------+\n175\t local input (per player) --+                         |\n176\t network 'me' messages -----+--> Hero controllers --> |  SIM (world W: heroes, monsters, generators,\n177\t bot (autopilot) -----------+                         |  items, projectiles, doors, timers, boss, score)\n178\t                                                      |        |  events (bus): hit, kill, pickup, door,\n179\t                                                      |        |  say, floor, magic, over ...\n180\t                                                      v        v\n181\t             VIEW (draw from W, or from puppets) <-- NET: local | host (snapshots+events out) | client (in)\n182\t                     HUD, narrator, audio, effects listen to the bus\n183\t```\n184\t\n185\t- **One simulation, one place.** The sim runs in `solo`, `local`, `attract`, `host` and `server` roles. A `client` runs no monster AI, no generators and no damage; it moves only its own hero (with the same controller and collision, for zero-lag control) and shows everything else from the host's snapshots.\n186\t- **Intents** are the only way anything drives a hero: `{ move: [x, y] (ground, length ≤ 1), aim: angle or null, fire: held, magic: pressed, plant: held }`. Local input, network messages and the bot all produce intents. This is what makes the bot, the attract mode, the tests and the netcode the same code path.\n187\t- **Entity ids:** every entity has an integer id. Static floor items get ids in reading order of the rows, so every copy derives the same ids from the same data and only removals travel over the network. Dynamic entities (monsters, drops, projectiles) take ids from the host's counter.\n188\t- **Damage pipeline (one function for everything):** `damage(target, amount, { by, kind: 'shot'|'melee'|'magic'|'blast'|'contact'|'drain'|'trap'|'fire' })` applies armor and immunities, recomputes monster rank, handles death, awards score and emits `hit`, `kill`, `hurt`.\n189\t- **Step order (each 1/120 s):** intents → heroes → generators → monsters → projectiles → features (traps, fields, timers) → pickups and doors → stairs → narrator triggers → net send. The view reads the result in `draw`.\n190\t- **Randomness:** gameplay draws from `rng.sim` (`E.rng(seed)`), cosmetic effects from `Math.random`. Tests seed both, so runs repeat exactly.\n191\t\n192\t### 3.4 Scenes and flow\n193\t\n194\t```\n195\tboot -> title --(10 s idle)--> attract (loops: demo floors -> high scores -> prologue -> title card) --(any input)--> title\n196\ttitle -> main menu: START DESCENT | HOW TO PLAY | HIGH SCORES | SETTINGS | ABOUT & CREDITS\n197\tSTART -> class select -> floor card -> play <-> pause menu (Resume, How to Play, Dev Tools, Drop out, Settings, Controls, Full screen, Quit)\n198\tplay -> floor card -> ... treasure room after floors 3 and 6 ... -> boss -> ending -> credits -> DESCENT II or title\n199\tall heroes down -> continue (10 s) -> yes: play | no: game over -> initials (each qualifying player) -> high scores -> title\n200\tAI Hub session: boot -> session card -> countdown 3-2-1 -> session play -> round over (stays until the hub removes the game)\n201\t```\n202\t\n203\tFront-end scenes (title, menu, class select, How to Play, High Scores, About) count as \"title/menu screens\" for the attract timer. Gameplay scenes are `pausable: true` outside sessions and `pausable: false` in them.\n204\t\n205\t### 3.5 Engine changes (the engine is ours to change; keep each one small and tested)\n206\t\n207\tRecord each in `ENGINE-CHANGES.md` (what, why, test). They feed the About screen's Engine Feedback.\n208\t\n209\t| # | Change | Why | Test |\n210\t|---|---|---|---|\n211\t| E1 | `FlowField.updateMany(points)`: a multi-source BFS seeded at every point at distance 0, rebuilt only when some point's cell or `map.version` changes; also fill `flow.src` (which point each cell is nearest to) | Monsters head for the *nearest* hero with one field for all (the recipe says one field; the engine's field takes one target) | Two targets: each cell's distance is the minimum of the two single-target fields; `src` is correct |\n212\t| E2 | Humanoid gear: `weapon: 'axe' \\| 'bow' \\| 'club' \\| 'pan' \\| 'scythe' \\| 'fork'`, `offhand: 'shield'`, `hat: 'horned'` (optional `'toque'`), drawn next to `'sword'` in `_drawHD` and `_drawClassic` (depth-sorted `ops`), with `tip()` lengths per weapon | The heroes' and monsters' identities (axe, shield, bow, pan, scythe, the King's fork) | Each rig draws in all three views with no errors; `tools/filmstrip.mjs` strips of each class's throw and melee look right |\n213\t| E3 | `Bullets`: `bounce: n` (reflect off TileMap walls on the axis that entered the wall, up to n times) and `onWall(b, cx, cy)` (called where a bullet dies on a wall) | The Ricochet amulet; shots that crack walls | A bullet fired at a wall comes back; `onWall` reports the right cell |\n214\t| E4 | Input: a `Pad9` press is ignored while `Pad8` is held | The hub's rule: Create + Options is the hub's, so the game ignores Options while Create is held | Press `Pad8`, then `Pad9`: `pressed('pause')` stays false |\n215\t| E5 | Settings: the `glyphs` default becomes `'playstation'`; its row also shows on the Settings screen (not only Controls); its `apply` sets every player's input | TASK.md: PlayStation glyphs by default, a Settings option for Xbox (A B X Y) | With `lastDevice = 'gamepad'`, `label('fire')` is `R2` and `label('confirm')` is `✕`; after `set('glyphs', 'xbox')` they are `RT` and `A` |\n216\t| E6 | Shell: a TV scale (theme `scale`, a CSS variable multiplying its pixel sizes; the game sets about 1.6 at 1080p and more on bigger screens), a `rows: [settingKeys]` field for any screen (the Dev pages), and settings groups whose name starts with `Dev` hidden from the standard Settings screen | The engine's HTML menus are 14 px: too small at 10 feet. Dev sliders need the same row widgets on their own screen | Headless: `ui.show('dev-tuning', { rows })` raises no error; browser: a 1920×1080 screenshot of Settings and Dev Tools reads at TV distance |\n217\t| E7 | Arcade: `cab.enter(score, mode, done, { input })` reads that player's input | Each qualifying player enters initials with their own controller | Player 2's input types the initials |\n218\t| E8 | Audio: `audio.bus('sfx' \\| 'music' \\| 'voice')` returns the gain node, with a new `voice` bus under the master and a standard `voices` volume setting | The Babble voices must follow the player's volume and mute | Headless: returns null without error; browser: muting silences voices |\n219\t\n220\tDon't change the engine's fixed step, scene system, or standard menus beyond these. If something else is needed, add it the same way: smallest change, a test, a line in `ENGINE-CHANGES.md`.\n221\t\n222\t### 3.6 Build and bundle (`build.mjs`)\n223\t\n224\t1. Concatenate `game/src/*.js` in name order inside `(() => { 'use strict'; ... })();` and write `game/game.js` (the dev page and the tests load this).\n225\t2. Read `hub/session.js` unmodified. Assert it starts with `/*! aihub-session` and that its SHA-256 equals the file fetched from the hub (keep the hash in `hub/session.sha256`). The hub replaces an unmodified client with each new version; an edited copy is not replaced.\n226\t3. Write the deliverable in this order:\n227\t   ```html\n228\t   <!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head>\n229\t   <meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n230\t   <script>/* hub/session.js, byte for byte */</script>\n231\t   <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">\n232\t   <title>Gauntletdown</title>\n233\t   <meta name=\"description\" content=\"...\">\n234\t   <meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n235\t   <meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n236\t   <meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n237\t   <meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"6\">\n238\t   <meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Score the most: treasure, kills and stairs. Don't starve.\">\n239\t   <meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Move WASD/stick · Aim mouse/right stick · Fire click/R2 · Magic right-click/△\">\n240\t   <style>html,body{margin:0;height:100%;background:#000;overflow:hidden}#screen{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;image-rendering:pixelated;touch-action:none}</style>\n241\t   </head><body>\n242\t   <!-- E.bootSplash('GAUNTLETDOWN') markup -->\n243\t   <canvas id=\"screen\"></canvas>\n244\t   <script>/* my-3d2dge.js (patched) */</script>\n245\t   <script>/* game/game.js */</script>\n246\t   </body></html>\n247\t   ```\n248\t4. Escape any `</script` inside inlined code (`<\\/script`). Assert the output has exactly one `<canvas id=\"screen\">`, the six hub metas, and the client as the first `<script>` right after `<meta charset>`.\n249\t5. The file opens from `file://` with no network requests (the browser test checks this).\n250\t\n251\t---\n252\t\n253\t## 4. Systems and mechanics (the spec)\n254\t\n255\tAll distances are world units (one tile = 16). Speeds are units per second. Every number marked † is a `TUNE` entry (4.24) and a Dev slider.\n256\t\n257\t### 4.1 Floors, the map and the legend\n258\t\n259\t- A floor is a `def('floors', id, { name, realm, no, music, par, rank, genRank, specials: [], amulets: [], intro: [...], next, rows: [...] })`. `rows` are ASCII strings, all the same width, bordered by walls. The parser builds an `E.TileMap` (wall types per realm, `cut: true, cutH: 6` so walls in front of the camera drop low; `ao: 6`), the entity lists, door groups, trap groups, transporter pairs and beams.\n260\t- **Wall height 24**, a little below a hero's head. Hero shots fly at z 12, so they pass over the banquet table (h 10) and are stopped by walls (the engine's `Bullets` already compare `map.heightAt` with the bullet's z).\n261\t- Corridors are at least 2 tiles wide; rooms 6–14 tiles across. Floors range from 40×20 (the tutorial) to 64×44.\n262\t\n263\t**The legend (shared by every floor):**\n264\t\n265\t| Char | Meaning | Char | Meaning |\n266\t|---|---|---|---|\n267\t| `#` | wall (realm stone) | `@` | hero start (author 4; fewer are padded on free neighbours) |\n268\t| `%` | accent wall (shelves, bone wall, iron) | `E` | stairs down (exit) |\n269\t| `X` | cracked wall (4 HP, shots break it) | `2`–`9` | skip stairs to floor N |\n270\t| `+` | door (iron bars); 4-connected runs open together | `O` | transporter pad (paired in reading order: 1st↔2nd, 3rd↔4th) |\n271\t| `T` | trap wall, removed when any `^` plate is stepped on | `!` | stun rune |\n272\t| `Y` | trap wall, removed when any `v` plate is stepped on | `s` | spikes (cycling) |\n273\t| `?` | fake wall: drawn as a wall, walkable (a secret) | `\\|` `-` | force-field beam, vertical / horizontal (pylons drawn where it meets walls) |\n274\t| `~` | lava or chasm (blocked floor, glows in the Furnace) | `^` `v` | pressure plates |\n275\t| `.` | floor | `,` | floor variant (rug, dirt, bone dust) |\n276\t| `k` | key | `f` | roast (+100, can't be shot) |\n277\t| `b` | loaf (+50, can't be shot) | `j` | cider jug (+100, shootable) |\n278\t| `z` | spoiled stew (poison, shootable) | `m` | Blast Flask (magic) |\n279\t| `u` | special potion (type from `meta.specials`, reading order) | `a` | amulet (type from `meta.amulets`, reading order) |\n280\t| `$` | gold | `*` | gem |\n281\t| `h` | chest | `l` | locked chest (needs a key) |\n282\t| `w` | crown | `B` | Dinner Bell |\n283\t| `g` `n` `o` `i` `y` `x` `t` | monsters: hungerghost, gnasher, pot-lobber, cinder imp, fryar, snatcher, the Tithe (rank from `meta.rank`) | `G` `N` `L` `I` `F` `S` | generators: ash urn, gnasher den, crockery hutch, ember grate, candle shrine, sack heap (rank from `meta.genRank`) |\n284\t| `K` | King Famish (boss floor) | `=` | banquet table (low wall, h 10) |\n285\t| `P` | feast platter (on a table cell; +200, shootable) | `U` | soup tureen (a boss-floor ghost generator, on the table) |\n286\t\n287\tPer-cell overrides go in `meta.ranks: { 'x,y': 3 }`, set pieces in `meta.props: [[shapeId, cx, cy, facing]]`, snatcher escape points and boss spawn points in `meta.points`.\n288\t\n289\t- **Automatic decoration:** a deterministic pass (`E.hash2(cx, cy)`) puts a torch (`r.prop('torch', ..., { light: true })`) on about one wall face in six along open floor, and 3–8 realm props per room against walls (Larder: barrels, kegs, sacks, crates, hanging hams; Ossuary: skulls, bones, coffins, candelabras, cobwebs, urns; Furnace: braziers, fire drums, anvils, chains). Props that block are made solid with `map.solid`; nothing is placed on a cell an entity, a plate or a path needs (the validator checks)."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01565e32-5dd5-4107-91e6-1b53667edea6","uuid":"59be60ef-a76c-4b50-b534-f47bbd3dbb71","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:28:40.684Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174804__x8cc180/work/PLAN.md","content":"| `05-text.js` | All player-facing text: narrator lines (5.6), story (5.1), floor intros, How to Play cards, class quips, About/Credits pages (Source Information and feedback filled in at the end) |\n| `10-heroes.js` | `def('heroes', ...)` ×4: stats, rig factory, shot, melee moves, magic power, voice |\n| `11-monsters.js` | `def('monsters', ...)` ×7 and `def('boss', 'famish', ...)`: stats per rank, AI kind, rig factory, generator kind, score |\n| `12-items.js` | `def('items', ...)` for every pickup, 7 special potions, 5 amulets: art, effect, shootable or not, points |\n| `13-art.js` | New art: string sprites, `E.SHAPES` entries (generators with damage states, doors, stairs, plates, pads, runes, pylons, bell, jug, platter, tureen), the `Shade` ghost rig class, realm palettes and materials |\n| `15..18-floors-*.js` | `def('floors', ...)`: rows and meta for each floor (5.5), one file per realm plus the banquet |\n| `20-level.js` | Floor parser (legend → TileMap, entity lists, door groups, trap groups, transporter pairs, exits, beams); automatic decoration (torches, props) from a hash; lights list; **`validateFloor()`**, shared with the tests |\n| `21-sim.js` | The world (`W`): state, step order, damage pipeline, scoring, kill and pickup events |\n| `22-sim-heroes.js` | Hero controller: intent → movement, aim, fire, smart melee, plant, magic; drain; pickups; doors; stairs; death and rising; amulets and specials |\n| `23-sim-monsters.js` | Monster AI kinds, flow fields (multi-source and single-source), separation, ranks |\n| `24-sim-generators.js` | Spawning, ranks, damage states, caps |\n| `25-sim-features.js` | Traps, transporters, stun runes, force fields, spikes, cracked and fake walls, impatience, treasure-room clock |\n| `26-sim-boss.js` | King Famish's fight as an `E.Script` (phases, attacks, waves, feast) |\n| `30-intents.js` | Intents from a local player's input (keyboard, mouse, gamepad), from the network, from the bot |\n| `31-bot.js` | The autopilot (attract mode, playthrough tests, Dev \"bot plays P1\") |\n| `40-net.js` | Net roles: local, host, client, server; snapshot and event encoding; client puppets and interpolation; rate limiting; area of interest |\n| `41-session.js` | The AI Hub flow: connect, own card, ready, start countdown, time-up, finish, end, leave |\n| `50-view.js` | Drawing: floor and walls, decoration, lights, entities (from the sim or from puppets), projectiles, reticle, x-ray, debug overlays |\n| `51-hud.js` | Player panels, captions, floor and realm cards, timers, edge arrows, prompts |\n| `52-narrator.js` | The callout queue: priority, cooldowns, captions, voice |\n| `53-audio.js` | Songs, sound-effect definitions, the **Babble** voice synth, dynamic music layers |\n| `60-scenes-front.js` | Title, main menu, class select, How to Play, High Scores, About/Credits, the touch-only notice |\n| `61-scenes-play.js` | Play (solo and local co-op), floor cards, treasure rooms, game over, continue, initials, ending, credits, Descent II |\n| `62-scenes-session.js` | Session scenes: card, countdown, play, round over, server |\n| `63-attract.js` | The attract-mode director |\n| `70-dev.js` | Dev Tools: cheats, warp, give and spawn, tuning sliders, overlays |\n| `80-debug.js` | `game.debug` (snapshot, teleport, warp, give, spawn, setTune, bot, netStats) and `game.stateHash` |\n| `99-start.js` | `game.start({ scenes, scene, boot })` |\n\nContent never edits the core: floors, monsters, items and lines are registry entries (the Emberdeep lesson), so the rest of the game can be built later by adding data in a text editor (`docs/DESIGNER.md` explains how).\n\n### 3.3 Runtime model: simulation, intents, view, network\n\n```\n           +---------------- intents ----------------+\n local input (per player) --+                         |\n network 'me' messages -----+--> Hero controllers --> |  SIM (world W: heroes, monsters, generators,\n bot (autopilot) -----------+                         |  items, projectiles, doors, timers, boss, score)\n                                                      |        |  events (bus): hit, kill, pickup, door,\n                                                      |        |  say, floor, magic, over ...\n                                                      v        v\n             VIEW (draw from W, or from puppets) <-- NET: local | host (snapshots+events out) | client (in)\n                     HUD, narrator, audio, effects listen to the bus\n```\n\n- **One simulation, one place.** The sim runs in `solo`, `local`, `attract`, `host` and `server` roles. A `client` runs no monster AI, no generators and no damage; it moves only its own hero (with the same controller and collision, for zero-lag control) and shows everything else from the host's snapshots.\n- **Intents** are the only way anything drives a hero: `{ move: [x, y] (ground, length ≤ 1), aim: angle or null, fire: held, magic: pressed, plant: held }`. Local input, network messages and the bot all produce intents. This is what makes the bot, the attract mode, the tests and the netcode the same code path.\n- **Entity ids:** every entity has an integer id. Static floor items get ids in reading order of the rows, so every copy derives the same ids from the same data and only removals travel over the network. Dynamic entities (monsters, drops, projectiles) take ids from the host's counter.\n- **Damage pipeline (one function for everything):** `damage(target, amount, { by, kind: 'shot'|'melee'|'magic'|'blast'|'contact'|'drain'|'trap'|'fire' })` applies armor and immunities, recomputes monster rank, handles death, awards score and emits `hit`, `kill`, `hurt`.\n- **Step order (each 1/120 s):** intents → heroes → generators → monsters → projectiles → features (traps, fields, timers) → pickups and doors → stairs → narrator triggers → net send. The view reads the result in `draw`.\n- **Randomness:** gameplay draws from `rng.sim` (`E.rng(seed)`), cosmetic effects from `Math.random`. Tests seed both, so runs repeat exactly.\n\n### 3.4 Scenes and flow\n\n```\nboot -> title --(10 s idle)--> attract (loops: demo floors -> high scores -> prologue -> title card) --(any input)--> title\ntitle -> main menu: START DESCENT | HOW TO PLAY | HIGH SCORES | SETTINGS | ABOUT & CREDITS\nSTART -> class select -> floor card -> play <-> pause menu (Resume, How to Play, Dev Tools, Drop out, Settings, Controls, Full screen, Quit)\nplay -> floor card -> ... treasure room after floors 3 and 6 ... -> boss -> ending -> credits -> DESCENT II or title\nall heroes down -> continue (10 s) -> yes: play | no: game over -> initials (each qualifying player) -> high scores -> title\nAI Hub session: boot -> session card -> countdown 3-2-1 -> session play -> round over (stays until the hub removes the game)\n```\n\nFront-end scenes (title, menu, class select, How to Play, High Scores, About) count as \"title/menu screens\" for the attract timer. Gameplay scenes are `pausable: true` outside sessions and `pausable: false` in them.\n\n### 3.5 Engine changes (the engine is ours to change; keep each one small and tested)\n\nRecord each in `ENGINE-CHANGES.md` (what, why, test). They feed the About screen's Engine Feedback.\n\n| # | Change | Why | Test |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| E1 | `FlowField.updateMany(points)`: a multi-source BFS seeded at every point at distance 0, rebuilt only when some point's cell or `map.version` changes; also fill `flow.src` (which point each cell is nearest to) | Monsters head for the *nearest* hero with one field for all (the recipe says one field; the engine's field takes one target) | Two targets: each cell's distance is the minimum of the two single-target fields; `src` is correct |\n| E2 | Humanoid gear: `weapon: 'axe' \\| 'bow' \\| 'club' \\| 'pan' \\| 'scythe' \\| 'fork'`, `offhand: 'shield'`, `hat: 'horned'` (optional `'toque'`), drawn next to `'sword'` in `_drawHD` and `_drawClassic` (depth-sorted `ops`), with `tip()` lengths per weapon | The heroes' and monsters' identities (axe, shield, bow, pan, scythe, the King's fork) | Each rig draws in all three views with no errors; `tools/filmstrip.mjs` strips of each class's throw and melee look right |\n| E3 | `Bullets`: `bounce: n` (reflect off TileMap walls on the axis that entered the wall, up to n times) and `onWall(b, cx, cy)` (called where a bullet dies on a wall) | The Ricochet amulet; shots that crack walls | A bullet fired at a wall comes back; `onWall` reports the right cell |\n| E4 | Input: a `Pad9` press is ignored while `Pad8` is held | The hub's rule: Create + Options is the hub's, so the game ignores Options while Create is held | Press `Pad8`, then `Pad9`: `pressed('pause')` stays false |\n| E5 | Settings: the `glyphs` default becomes `'playstation'`; its row also shows on the Settings screen (not only Controls); its `apply` sets every player's input | TASK.md: PlayStation glyphs by default, a Settings option for Xbox (A B X Y) | With `lastDevice = 'gamepad'`, `label('fire')` is `R2` and `label('confirm')` is `✕`; after `set('glyphs', 'xbox')` they are `RT` and `A` |\n| E6 | Shell: a TV scale (theme `scale`, a CSS variable multiplying its pixel sizes; the game sets about 1.6 at 1080p and more on bigger screens), a `rows: [settingKeys]` field for any screen (the Dev pages), and settings groups whose name starts with `Dev` hidden from the standard Settings screen | The engine's HTML menus are 14 px: too small at 10 feet. Dev sliders need the same row widgets on their own screen | Headless: `ui.show('dev-tuning', { rows })` raises no error; browser: a 1920×1080 screenshot of Settings and Dev Tools reads at TV distance |\n| E7 | Arcade: `cab.enter(score, mode, done, { input })` reads that player's input | Each qualifying player enters initials with their own controller | Player 2's input types the initials |\n| E8 | Audio: `audio.bus('sfx' \\| 'music' \\| 'voice')` returns the gain node, with a new `voice` bus under the master and a standard `voices` volume setting | The Babble voices must follow the player's volume and mute | Headless: returns null without error; browser: muting silences voices |\n\nDon't change the engine's fixed step, scene system, or standard menus beyond these. If something else is needed, add it the same way: smallest change, a test, a line in `ENGINE-CHANGES.md`.\n\n### 3.6 Build and bundle (`build.mjs`)\n\n1. Concatenate `game/src/*.js` in name order inside `(() => { 'use strict'; ... })();` and write `game/game.js` (the dev page and the tests load this).\n2. Read `hub/session.js` unmodified. Assert it starts with `/*! aihub-session` and that its SHA-256 equals the file fetched from the hub (keep the hash in `hub/session.sha256`). The hub replaces an unmodified client with each new version; an edited copy is not replaced.\n3. Write the deliverable in this order:\n   ```html\n   <!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head>\n   <meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n   <script>/* hub/session.js, byte for byte */</script>\n   <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">\n   <title>Gauntletdown</title>\n   <meta name=\"description\" content=\"...\">\n   <meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n   <meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n   <meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n   <meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"6\">\n   <meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Score the most: treasure, kills and stairs. Don't starve.\">\n   <meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Move WASD/stick · Aim mouse/right stick · Fire click/R2 · Magic right-click/△\">\n   <style>html,body{margin:0;height:100%;background:#000;overflow:hidden}#screen{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;image-rendering:pixelated;touch-action:none}</style>\n   </head><body>\n   <!-- E.bootSplash('GAUNTLETDOWN') markup -->\n   <canvas id=\"screen\"></canvas>\n   <script>/* my-3d2dge.js (patched) */</script>\n   <script>/* game/game.js */</script>\n   </body></html>\n   ```\n4. Escape any `</script` inside inlined code (`<\\/script`). Assert the output has exactly one `<canvas id=\"screen\">`, the six hub metas, and the client as the first `<script>` right after `<meta charset>`.\n5. The file opens from `file://` with no network requests (the browser test checks this).\n\n---\n\n## 4. Systems and mechanics (the spec)\n\nAll distances are world units (one tile = 16). Speeds are units per second. Every number marked † is a `TUNE` entry (4.24) and a Dev slider.\n\n### 4.1 Floors, the map and the legend\n\n- A floor is a `def('floors', id, { name, realm, no, music, par, rank, genRank, specials: [], amulets: [], intro: [...], next, rows: [...] })`. `rows` are ASCII strings, all the same width, bordered by walls. The parser builds an `E.TileMap` (wall types per realm, `cut: true, cutH: 6` so walls in front of the camera drop low; `ao: 6`), the entity lists, door groups, trap groups, transporter pairs and beams.\n- **Wall height 24**, a little below a hero's head. Hero shots fly at z 12, so they pass over the banquet table (h 10) and are stopped by walls (the engine's `Bullets` already compare `map.heightAt` with the bullet's z).\n- Corridors are at least 2 tiles wide; rooms 6–14 tiles across. Floors range from 40×20 (the tutorial) to 64×44.\n\n**The legend (shared by every floor):**\n\n| Char | Meaning | Char | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `#` | wall (realm stone) | `@` | hero start (author 4; fewer are padded on free neighbours) |\n| `%` | accent wall (shelves, bone wall, iron) | `E` | stairs down (exit) |\n| `X` | cracked wall (4 HP, shots break it) | `2`–`9` | skip stairs to floor N |\n| `+` | door (iron bars); 4-connected runs open together | `O` | transporter pad (paired in reading order: 1st↔2nd, 3rd↔4th) |\n| `T` | trap wall, removed when any `^` plate is stepped on | `!` | stun rune |\n| `Y` | trap wall, removed when any `v` plate is stepped on | `s` | spikes (cycling) |\n| `?` | fake wall: drawn as a wall, walkable (a secret) | `\\|` `-` | force-field beam, vertical / horizontal (pylons drawn where it meets walls) |\n| `~` | lava or chasm (blocked floor, glows in the Furnace) | `^` `v` | pressure plates |\n| `.` | floor | `,` | floor variant (rug, dirt, bone dust) |\n| `k` | key | `f` | roast (+100, can't be shot) |\n| `b` | loaf (+50, can't be shot) | `j` | cider jug (+100, shootable) |\n| `z` | spoiled stew (poison, shootable) | `m` | Blast Flask (magic) |\n| `u` | special potion (type from `meta.specials`, reading order) | `a` | amulet (type from `meta.amulets`, reading order) |\n| `$` | gold | `*` | gem |\n| `h` | chest | `l` | locked chest (needs a key) |\n| `w` | crown | `B` | Dinner Bell |\n| `g` `n` `o` `i` `y` `x` `t` | monsters: hungerghost, gnasher, pot-lobber, cinder imp, fryar, snatcher, the Tithe (rank from `meta.rank`) | `G` `N` `L` `I` `F` `S` | generators: ash urn, gnasher den, crockery hutch, ember grate, candle shrine, sack heap (rank from `meta.genRank`) |\n| `K` | King Famish (boss floor) | `=` | banquet table (low wall, h 10) |\n| `P` | feast platter (on a table cell; +200, shootable) | `U` | soup tureen (a boss-floor ghost generator, on the table) |\n\nPer-cell overrides go in `meta.ranks: { 'x,y': 3 }`, set pieces in `meta.props: [[shapeId, cx, cy, facing]]`, snatcher escape points and boss spawn points in `meta.points`.\n\n- **Automatic decoration:** a deterministic pass (`E.hash2(cx, cy)`) puts a torch (`r.prop('torch', ..., { light: true })`) on about one wall face in six along open floor, and 3–8 realm props per room against walls (Larder: barrels, kegs, sacks, crates, hanging hams; Ossuary: skulls, bones, coffins, candelabras, cobwebs, urns; Furnace: braziers, fire drums, anvils, chains). Props that block are made solid with `map.solid`; nothing is placed on a cell an entity, a plate or a path needs (the validator checks).","numLines":150,"startLine":140,"totalLines":1027}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Xj2gfTNX5RWYpwmkWWKRxg","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
