ntrols (§6); every rule and number (§7); content"," (§9); build order (§17); risks (§18); tests (§19); the done list (§21)."," ","+**Working rules on this machine (from TASK.md):** keep every dev file in the dev subfolder; read no files outside what","+the build needs (other agents share the directory, ports and processes); prefer `file://` and the engine's headless","+tools; a server (only the AI Hub harness needs one) binds `127.0.0.1` on a port the OS picks, and you confirm the page","+is yours before trusting a result; stop only processes you started, by PID (never `pkill`, `killall`, `fuser -k`).","+"," **Hard requirements from TASK.md, and where this plan covers each:**"," "," | TASK.md asks for | Where |"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174831__x898ed5/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":1783,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1783,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":8500,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"c28e7abf-db6e-401a-a911-43ba9983a968\",\"uuid\":\"7f32a228-a2cb-410b-aedb-9a3ff801b5b9\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":8650,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"c28e7abf-db6e-401a-a911-43ba9983a968\",\"uuid\":\"70d6f347-ec39-4114-9d7e-8821d64aef1a\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":8700,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":50,\"session_id\":\"c28e7abf-db6e-401a-a911-43ba9983a968\",\"uuid\":\"c212489f-2474-4b5e-8f85-8f02556cbed2\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":8800,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"c28e7abf-db6e-401a-a911-43ba9983a968\",\"uuid\":\"4a42bef3-bf26-4f1f-889e-e3ce97bca183\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-182910__x9a2bbb/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":132,"oldLines":3,"newStart":132,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":1450,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"2adef66c-4a6d-4909-bb60-db906fac5610\",\"uuid\":\"dd37f40b-49d5-4873-ae19-3b0224baf06a\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":1600,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"2adef66c-4a6d-4909-bb60-db906fac5610\",\"uuid\":\"00db8d1e-7dfe-48bf-8d5d-30c3c8ccd84b\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":1700,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"2adef66c-4a6d-4909-bb60-db906fac5610\",\"uuid\":\"53502e49-0c9c-4e1b-8fd5-a63902255542\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":1800,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"2adef66c-4a6d-4909-bb60-db906fac5610\",\"uuid\":\"f38e117b-90d5-40c7-a250-73a203b6c6bc\"}"]}]}],"moreFiles":2,"changedFiles":["/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174734__xb43d63/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174807__x5c5240/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174810__xbd1c73/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174828__xe9c1ea/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174828__xe9c1ea/work/PLAN.md","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174831__x898ed5/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-182910__x9a2bbb/agent.out"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01PoFJRaFZuoVnpGNh1EsvKK","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2MknBzetCpuNVucTKi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written `PLAN.md` (about 1,000 lines) for **Gauntletdown**. I brainstormed 50 riffs on \"Gauntlet\" and picked index 30 with Python's `secrets.randbelow`. The name works three ways: a challenge thrown down, a dungeon that only goes down, and a \"let-down\" for anyone who skips dinner.\n\n**The game.** A co-op dungeon crawler for 1–4 players, seen from the engine's three-quarter overhead view (top-down and isometric are options in Settings). The heroes are original:\n- **Heroes:** a Berserker with an axe, a Shieldmaiden with a shield, a Ranger with a bow and a Hexer with a staff.\n- **Core loop:** health drains every second and food restores it. Generators breed monsters, which shrink a rank each time they're wounded. Keys open whole runs of doors, and a magic flask hits everything on screen.\n- **Gauntlet's quirks kept:** you can shoot the food by mistake, and a reaper only magic can kill. Taking too long opens the doors and then turns every wall into stairs.\n- **Narrator:** \"The Gaunt\" calls out in the arcade announcer's style with original lines, spoken as deep gibberish under big captions.\n\n**What the plan covers:**\n- **Architecture:** a module map for one bundled file, and one simulation that local players, network messages and a bot all drive the same way. That makes attract mode, the tests and the netcode one code path.\n- **Engine changes:** eight small, tested ones. Examples: monsters pathing to the nearest of several heroes, new weapons (axe, bow, shield, scythe), bouncing shots, PlayStation button prompts by default, and bigger menu text for TVs.\n- **Systems:** each with numbers, including the controls for DualSense, Xbox and keyboard/mouse, the HUD, menus, dev mode with live sliders, the 10-second attract mode, and the touch-only notice.\n- **Online:** AI Hub shared-world sessions, with the message formats and rate and size budgets set out.\n- **Content:** the story beats, 7 monsters plus a three-phase boss, King Famish, every item, 9 floors, 2 treasure rooms, and all narrator lines. Floor 1 is a complete map; I ran a script on it to confirm the stairs can be reached with the floor's own key. The other floors have detailed briefs for the builder to author.\n- **Build order:** milestones M0–M12, with online play built second, on floor 1, because it's the riskiest part. There's a fallback to the hub's simpler \"ghost\" mode if it can't pass the hub's test harness, and a short list of extras that can be dropped whole.\n- **Risks:** each one has a mitigation.\n- **Testing:** one command that prints only failures and a count. It covers floor validation, per-system checks, a scripted bot playthrough of the whole game, network tests with simulated lag and loss, the hub's own four harness runs, and browser checks.\n- **Exit interview:** a prefilled `exit-interview.json`.\n\n**Things to know:**\n- **Multiplayer reading:** I read \"for the game on its own\" as solo and couch co-op outside the hub, since the hub's rules forbid any other networking. The plan says so up front.\n- **Hub harness keys:** its letter keys arrive in a form the engine ignores, so only its arrow keys and Enter register in the game. That's still enough to pass its checks; the plan notes this so builders aren't surprised.\n- **Machine note:** `/tmp` here was 99% full while I worked. The plan tells builders to point Chromium's temp folder into the dev folder.\n\nI removed my temporary research clones; the run folder now holds only `PLAN.md` alongside the given files."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":986,"cache_read_input_tokens":502051,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":986},"output_tokens":751,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01565e32-5dd5-4107-91e6-1b53667edea6","uuid":"26896e8c-bb23-48ae-a36a-c1b9a0a9f557","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:31:42.420Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh2MkWob7tJLLW1Jxs4X"}
